Question 21: Given m = np.arange(1, 10).reshape(3, 3), add the row [10, 20, 30] to every row. Then add the column [[100], [200], [300]] to every column.

AIM: Adding rows and columns to existing array.

Code:
import numpy as np
m=np.arange(1, 10).reshape(3, 3)
row=np.array([10, 20, 30])
col=np.array([[100], [200], [300]])
print(m+row)
print("\n",m+col)

Output:
 [[11 22 33]
 [14 25 36]
 [17 28 39]]

 [[101 102 103]
 [204 205 206]
 [307 308 309]]

Explanation:
Direct addition of 1d array to given n-dimensional array results in addition of 1d array to the n-dimensional array along its axis.
(Numpy broadcasting automatically adjusts the dimensions of the array.)
